From: Kartheek E <karte@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: fix dual-home channel on FH re-enable after EP move

Two fixes for the case where the EP has connected on a channel that
differs from the radio's startup default and FH is then re-enabled:

1. s_doAddLink: refresh per-BSS config files before addBssConf so the
   channel written into hostapd matches the radio's current operating
   channel (not the stale startup default).

2. s_syncOnEpStartConn: widen the early-return guard from
   isApplied == SWL_TRL_TRUE to isApplied != SWL_TRL_FALSE so that a
   channel switch that is in-flight (CSA) or queued (cold-apply) also
   skips the FH-disable path, preventing a double-disable that leaves
   hostapd in an inconsistent state and triggers a dual-home channel.

Signed-off-by: Kartheek E <karte@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
@@ -679,6 +679,11 @@ static bool s_doAddLink(T_AccessPoint* pAP, T_Radio* pRad)
     wld_rad_hostapd_setMiscParams(pRad);
     wifiGen_hapd_restoreMainIface(pRad);

+    /* Refresh per-BSS config files so the channel matches the radio's current
+     * operating channel (which may differ from the startup default when the EP
+     * connected on a different channel before FH was enabled). */
+    wld_hostapd_cfgFile_updatePerBssConfigs(pRad);
+
     SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: adding BSS config for AP %s", pRad->Name, pAP->alias);
     swl_rc_ne rc = wld_ap_hostapd_addBssConf(pAP);
     if(!swl_rc_isOk(rc)) {
@@ -1969,7 +1974,10 @@ static void s_syncOnEpStartConn(void* userData, char* ifName, const char* ssid,
                                );
             wld_chanmgt_setTargetChanspec(pRad, chanSpec, true, CHAN_REASON_EP_MOVE, "ep preConnect");
             if((swl_typeChanspec_equals(wld_chanmgt_getTgtChspec(pRad), chanSpec)) &&
-               (pRad->targetChanspec.isApplied == SWL_TRL_TRUE)) {
+               (pRad->targetChanspec.isApplied != SWL_TRL_FALSE)) {
+                /* Channel switch was initiated (CSA in-flight or cold-apply queued):
+                 * skip disabling FH here to avoid a double-disable that would leave
+                 * hostapd in an inconsistent state and trigger a dual-home channel. */
                 return;
             }
         }
